  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Continued Response to War in Ukraine 2023-2024 (EA31-2023)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As the war in Ukraine has grown protracted and destruction of communities continues, many displaced and other violence-affected households struggle to meet their basic needs, access basic services, and cope with psychosocial stress.

Caritas SPES will engage 32 local implementing partners in the proposed response, comprising teams at the diocese 7 and parish (level). Together these 32 partners, supported by the National Office, will provide assistance in 16 oblasts across Ukraine. The proposed response targets vulnerable displaced and war-affected households across the country, building on the experienced gained by local implementation units during the first year of the CSU response to the humanitarian crisis in Ukraine. Activities will cover food/NFI distributions, shelter, soup kitchens, cash assistance, and vouchers.</narrative>
  </description>
